no-reversed-links (MD011), Links and images
On by default, severity warning. Fixable.

Inline links put the text in brackets and the URL in parentheses: [text](url).

Why: The reversed form (text)[url] is not a link, so its brackets and
parentheses show as text.

Tags: links

This rule has no options.

Fix: The fix swaps the two parts into the [text](url) form. gomdlint may report
a finding without a fix when the fix would change a line with one character in
brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it up to a blank line, because
it could add or remove a task list checkbox.

This document breaks the rule:
  | # Guide
  |
  | See the (installation guide)[docs/install.md].

gomdlint reports:
  3:9 Reversed link syntax detected

The fix changes it to:
  | # Guide
  |
  | See the [installation guide](docs/install.md).

Under rules, no-reversed-links: false turns the rule off and
no-reversed-links: error reports its findings as errors. The flag
--disable no-reversed-links turns it off for one run.

Silence one line:
  <!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line no-reversed-links -->

markdownlint: https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint/blob/v0.41.1/doc/md011.md
